  "estimatedMinutes": 2,
  "statement": "If \\(r\\gt0,\\) then for all \\(p\\) and \\(q\\) such that \\(pq\\ne0\\) and \\(pr\\gt qr,\\) we have:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(-p\\gt-q\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(-p\\gt q\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(1\\gt-\\frac{q}{p}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(1\\lt \\frac{q}{p}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "None of these"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "e",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1970-p17.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Since \\(r\\gt0,\\) the hypothesis is equivalent to \\(p\\gt q.\\) Then \\(-p\\lt-q,\\) so A is false. Taking \\((p,q)=(2,1)\\) makes B and D false. Taking \\((p,q)=(1,-2)\\) makes C false because \\(-\\frac{q}{p}=2.\\) Thus none of A-D follows in every case.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Because \\(r\\gt0,\\) the hypothesis gives only \\(p\\gt q\\)",
        "Test the remaining claims with both positive and negative choices of \\(p,q\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
